+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The triage agent that fronts the support chat was defined without a session store, so Genkit treats it as client-managed and rejects any chat resumed by sessionId with FAILED_PRECONDITION.",
+  "evidence": "Calling triage.chat({ sessionId }) before the fix threw \"Cannot use 'sessionId' with agent 'triage': this agent has no store configured (client-managed state)\", while refundAgent, which declares store, did not throw; after adding store to triage, a two-turn test (\"My order is A-1001.\" then resuming by sessionId with \"What is its status?\") answered with A-1001's shipped status. Adding store to orderAgent instead was rejected because it would make the agents middleware stop forwarding history to it, losing the order id."
+}
